          "filename": "Nigg Bay - geograph.org.uk - 847399.jpg",
          "caption": "Nigg Bay Nigg Bay, with the ruins of the former fishing station in the background, and further in the distance, Girdleness Lighthouse.\n\"This old fishing station is a small granite-built dwelling, with a later harled\nbrick extension, is visible on Ordnance Survey maps\nfrom the first edition of 1867 onwards. On the 1901\nversion, a well is marked nearby and even today the\nremains of a slipway can be seen. Local people recall it\nbeing used seasonally by lobster and crab fisherman\n\nup until the 1960s\" [Source - Aberdeen Council].",
